# Technology Stack — Shortly

## Stack Overview

| Layer | Technology | Role |
|---|---|---|
| **Language** | JavaScript (JSX) | No TypeScript, ESM modules |
| **Runtime** | React 19 | UI with React Compiler (auto-memoization) |
| **Build** | Vite | Dev/bundler with `@vitejs/plugin-react` + Babel |
| **Styling** | Tailwind CSS v4 | CSS-first utility framework via PostCSS |
| **Component Lib** | DaisyUI v5 | Semantic classes + themes (CSS plugin) |
| **State** | Zustand | Lightweight global state |
| **Routing** | React Router v7 | Client-side, nested layouts |
| **Icons** | @iconify/react | On-demand SVG via `<Icon icon="..." />` |
| **Class Utils** | clsx + tailwind-merge | `cn()` for conditional + merged classes |
| **Variants** | CVA | Configurable component variations |
| **Notifications** | sileo | Toast via adapter (`_core/utils/toast/`) |
| **Theme** | theme-change | DaisyUI `data-theme` toggling |
| **Lint** | ESLint v9 (Flat Config) | Code quality |
| **Format** | Prettier + prettier-plugin-tailwindcss | Code formatting + Tailwind class sorting |
| **Package** | pnpm | Package management |
| **Deploy** | gh-pages | GitHub Pages (`/shortly/` base path) |

> Exact versions live in `package.json` — single source of truth.

## Conventions

### React Compiler
- No manual `useMemo`, `useCallback`, or `React.memo` — compiler auto-memoizes.
- Exception: compiler can't handle non-hook-compliant callbacks to third-party libs.
- `react/prop-types` is **off** — not needed with the compiler.

### Styling (Tailwind v4 + DaisyUI)
- DaisyUI is a **CSS plugin** (`@plugin 'daisyui'` in `index.css`), not a Tailwind config plugin.
- No `tailwind.config.js` — all customization in `src/index.css` via `@theme` (tokens), `@utility`, and `@plugin 'daisyui/theme'`.
- The `theme-change` library toggles `data-theme` on `<html>`.
- Font: Poppins via `@font-face` (TTF in `src/assets/font/`). Weights: 400,500,600,700. **`font-weight-normal` is 500** (not 400).
- Prettier plugin has `tailwindFunctions: ['clsx', 'tw']` so `class-variance-authority` and `clsx` calls get class sorting.

### Class Handling
- Always `cn()` (clsx + tailwind-merge) for conditional classes + parent `className` merging.
- Never string-concatenate classes.
- CVA for complex atoms (Button, Input, Card) with `defaultVariants`.

### Mutation Feedback
- Always through the toast adapter (`_core/utils/toast/toast-adapter.js`) — never import sileo or any toast lib directly outside the adapter.
- `<ToastProvider />` at app root once.

### Build & Config
- Production base path: `/shortly/` — never hardcode, use `import.meta.env`.
- ESLint is flat config (`eslint.config.js`) — no `.eslintrc` files.
- Path alias `@/` → `src/` (configured in `vite.config.js` + `jsconfig.json`).

### Architecture
- No TypeScript — plain JS with JSDoc only when cross-module types need clarity.
- `sileo` (NOT react-hot-toast) is the actual toast lib. react-hot-toast remains in package.json as dead code — do not import it.
